What I learned



I learned how to use CSS Grid to create a complex card layout where some cards span multiple columns:

css
.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 24px;
}

.card-large {
  grid-column: span 2;
}

I also practiced using semantic HTML elements like <article>, <blockquote> and <cite> for testimonial cards:

html
<article class="card">
  <blockquote>
    <p>"An amazing experience that changed my career."</p>
    <cite>— Daniel Clifford</cite>
  </blockquote>
</article>


Continued development

I want to get more comfortable with CSS Grid and complex layouts
I need to practice responsive design and media queries more
I want to improve my attention to detail when matching designs pixel-perfectly

AI Collaboration

I used Claude (by Anthropic) as a learning partner throughout this project.

What worked well: Getting instant feedback on why my layout was broken and understanding the difference between grid-column: span 2 and grid-column: 1 / 3.


